Subject: [PATCH 07700/11362] [outer-loop] ARC oracle-perception ablation
 RESULT: correct entities flip goal induction 0/8 -> 7/8 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5832)

Decisive positive gating the perception-fix direction. Same gemma-4-31B, same
learned rules, 3 perception conditions: naive 0/8 goals correct (replicates the
diagnosis), oracle (correct entities + HUD labeled) 7/8 correct + 1 partial, 0 wrong.
The goal-hypothesis generator is NOT the bottleneck -- it produces the true win
condition the instant perception delivers the right entities. bp35 shows both halves
matter: adding entities alone did not flip it, only labeling the row-63 bar as a
lose-timer did -> build BOTH a mover/entity detector AND a HUD-register detector.

Honest scope: this is goal-hypothesis correctness, not level discovery; execution
still needs the dynamics model. Confirms GAP-ARC-PERCEPTION-HUD-VS-BOARD as THE lever.

